.TH SCENE 1
.SH NAME
scene, scenedemo, scenereplay \- show a 2-D scene in a window; drive a scene with a demo or a recording
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/scene
[
.I dir
]
.PP
.B scenedemo
[
.B -n
.I ticks
] [
.B -d
.I ms
] [
.I dir
]
.PP
.B scenereplay
[
.B -t
.I start
] [
.B -x
.I rate
] [
.I recording
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Scene
shows the scene in
.I dir
(default
.BR /mnt/scene )
in a window: entities, features and layers in a geo or xy frame, with
trails, headings, stale dimming and labels that do not overlap, drawn
by
.IR scene (2).
The directory may be a
.IR scenefs (4)
mount, when the view is live and shared: the window follows the
server's camera and writes its own pan, zoom and selection back to its
.BR ctl ,
so every viewer, and any agent, sees the same picture.
A plain directory of stanza files works too, with a local camera.
.PP
It is an ordinary window: it runs under
.IR wm (1),
in a Lucifer activity, where the activity's agent can picture it with
its
.B window
tool, or in a Matrix
.B app
region:
.IP
.EX
top app /dis/wm/scene.dis /mnt/scene
.EE
.PP
Drag pans, the wheel zooms about the pointer, a click selects;
.BR + ,
.B -
zoom,
.BR h ,
.BR j ,
.BR k ,
.B l
pan,
.B f
fits; button 3 gives a menu.
.PP
.I Scenedemo
writes a synthetic field survey \(em rovers mowing lanes, a relay, a
base and its radio range \(em as records to
.IB dir /log
(default
.BR /mnt/scene ),
one tick per second of scene time, every
.I ms
milliseconds (default 200; 0 as fast as possible), for
.I ticks
ticks (default: forever).
.PP
.I Scenereplay
plays a recording \(em what a
.IR scenefs (4)
.B changes
file reads \(em back as records on its standard output (from its
standard input when no
.I recording
is named).
It writes the scene as it stood at
.I start
(default: the first time in the recording) as one batch, then each
tick's records as one write, paced by the recording's clock:
.I rate
2 plays at twice its speed, 0 as fast as the reader takes it.
Where the clock runs backwards, as it does after a
.BR clear ,
the pacing starts again from there.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
mkdir -p /mnt/scene
mount -c {scenefs} /mnt/scene
scenedemo &
wm/scene
.EE
.PP
Record a run, then show it again from two minutes in, at double speed:
.IP
.EX
cat /mnt/scene/changes > /tmp/run.scene &
\&...
scenereplay -t 120 -x 2 /tmp/run.scene > /mnt/scene/log
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/scene.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/scenedemo.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/scenereplay.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR scenefs (4),
.IR scene (2),
.IR wmsrv (2)
